content:
The syntax error was the use of an undeclared signal `d_last` — it was never declared as a reg/wire, so the elaborator could not bind it. The fix is to declare `reg [31:0] d_last;` and update it each clock with the previous value of `in`, so that `~in & d_last` detects the 1→0 transition.

```verilog
module top_module(
	input clk,
	input reset,
	input [31:0] in,
	output reg [31:0] out);

	reg [31:0] d_last;

	always @(posedge clk)
	begin
		if (reset)
			out <= 0;
		else
			out <= out | (~in & d_last);

		d_last <= in;
	end

endmodule
```
